service: dns
slug: steeringpolicyattachment
kind: SteeringPolicyAttachment
archetype: generated-service-manager
status/finalizer: required /
retain-until-confirmed-delete
requeue: provisioning, terminating
provider states: create CREATING; update none;
delete DELETING
follow-up: create=read-after-write;
update=read-after-write; delete=confirm-delete
supported drift: displayName
reject before mutate: force-new fields
steeringPolicyId, zoneId, domainName
create-only fields: none
list lookup: oci_dns_steering_policy_attachments
filters steeringPolicyId, zoneId, domainName;
Adopt only a unique attachment matching the
policy, zone, and domain.
conflicts: none
open gaps: none
CREATING requeues and ACTIVE succeeds;
displayName updates settle without a distinct
update lifecycle state.
List requests resolve compartmentId from the
parent steering policy before applying policy,
zone, and domain selectors.
Delete treats an auth-shaped Get 404 as
ambiguous until the scoped attachment list is
empty, then synthesizes the DELETED terminal
outcome.
Attachment identity fields require replacement
and no Kubernetes Secret side effects are
present.
